  "title": "Erdős Problem #1092",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f_r(n)$ be maximal such that, if a graph $G$ has the property that every subgraph $H$ on $m$ vertices is the union of a graph with chromatic number $r$ and a graph with $\\leq f_r(m)$ edges, then $G$ has chromatic number $\\leq r+1$.\nIs it true that $f_2(n) \\gg n$? More generally, is $f_r(n)\\gg_r n$?",
